\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{One chiral zero mode}
\date{2026-11-23}

\p{On #{\mathbb C^2} take an orthonormal basis #{v,w} with
#{\Gamma v=v}, #{\Gamma w=-w}. For #{a>0} the overlap
operator #{D=a^{-1}(\bbI -\Gamma)} of \ref{fdip-0149} has
#{Dv=0}, #{Dw=2a^{-1}w} and modified grading #{\Gamma'=\bbI}.
Its ordinary kernel is the positive line, of index #{1}.}

\p{The original grading contributes #{1-1=0} to #{d}, the
modified grading #{2-0=2}. The two generators in the term of
#{\theta_D} for #{w} acquire factors #{u^{-1}} and #{u} under
the modified rotation. Using the original grading twice would
give #{u^{-2}} on that term. By \ref{fdip-014L} the modified
rotation multiplies the top word by #{u^2} and the inverse
coefficient pullback multiplies the functional by #{u^{-2}}.
On the unit circle its stabilizer is #{\{1,-1\}}.}
